CREATED:20260303T221327Z
DESCRIPTION:Master the human side of change-and move people forward with c
 onfidence\n\nChange isn't just a process\; it's an emotional journey. Gro
 unded in the renowned grief-stage research of Elisabeth Kübler Ross\, thi
 s workshop gives leaders a practical\, human-centered model for guiding i
 ndividuals and teams through the predictable phases of organizational cha
 nge.\n\nParticipants won't just learn about change styles-they will devel
 op a toolkit they can use immediately to diagnose where people are\, resp
 ond effectively\, and help themselves and others move through resistance\
 , uncertainty\, and renewal.\n\nParticipants will:\n• Understand the chan
 ge journey through a proven\, research based model\n• Explore and debate 
 the stages of change-and how they show up at work\n• Learn to recognize e
 ach stage and respond with the right leadership approach\n• Identify wher
 e they are on the change curve in real time\n• Build an action plan to he
 lp themselves and others move forward\n\nTarget audience: SOM faculty lea
 ding or managing others\n\nREGISTRATION IS REQUIRED VIA THE LINK FOR MORE
  INFORMATION. \n\nSpace is limited.
DURATION:PT3H30M
