CREATED:20260312T135259Z
DESCRIPTION:The All of Us Research Program is a national initiative that h
 as assembled one of the largest and most comprehensive biomedical dataset
 s ever created\, including genomic variants\, electronic health records\,
  survey responses\, physical measurements\, and wearables data from over 
 one million participants across the United States. This dataset offers ex
 traordinary potential for health equity\, population health\, and precisi
 on medicine research - and this workshop will show you how to access and 
 use it.\n\nThis half-day virtual workshop is open to open to all members 
 of the Duke University research community\, including faculty\, postdocto
 ral researchers\, graduate students\, clinicians\, residents/fellows\, an
 d research staff. Register at https://duke.is/AllOfUs
DURATION:PT6H
DTSTAMP:20260318T181535Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T090000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260318T181535Z
